    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> 7</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="236" ed="#liebermann"/>Et diximus de mercatoribus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_7.lnote.oe.1"/>, qui falsum et lacum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_7.lnote.oe.2"/> afferunt ad portum, ut aduocent, si possint.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="7" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="76" ed="#robertson"/>Et diximus de mercatoribus qui falsum et lacum<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_7.robnote.fn.2"/> afferunt ad portum, ut advocent si possint.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="237" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wir haben bestimmt über Kaufleute, welche falsches und mangelhaftes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_7.lnote.de.1"/> [Geld] zur Stadt bringen, dass sie, wenn sie können, sich auf den Gewährsmann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_7.lnote.de.2"/> berufen [von dem sie es bekamen].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And we have determined concerning merchants who bring false and defective [money] to the town, that they appeal to the warrantor [from whom they got it], if they can.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="77" ed="#robertson"/>And we have decreed with regard to traders who bring money which is defective in quality and weight to the town, that they shall name a warrantor if they can.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="329"><ref target="clause:IIIAtr_8">III Atr 8</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_7.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">236</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">merc. qui <hi rend="italic">doppelt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">merc. qui twice Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_7.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">236</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">laccum <hi rend="italic">MHk;</hi> lactum <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">laccum MHk; lactum Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_7.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Im Original stand vielleicht das Subst. <hi rend="italic">lac</hi>, ein Lehnwort, das Wörterbücher allerdings erst seit 13. Jh. im Englischen nachweisen. Dagegen meint Q ein Adjektiv, das, Nordischem entlehnt, im Anglolatein vorkommt; Fleta I 22, 6; Spelman. <hi rend="italic">Glossar</hi> s. v. <hi rend="italic">lacta; Munim. Gildhal</hi>. III 391</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The original perhaps had the noun <hi rend="italic">lac</hi>, a loanword which, however, dictionaries attest in English only from the 13th cent. Q, on the other hand, means an adjective which, borrowed from Norse, occurs in Anglo-Latin; Fleta I 22, 6; Spelman. <hi rend="italic">Glossar</hi> s. v. <hi rend="italic">lacta; Munim. Gildhal</hi>. III 391</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_7.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">166</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Im Original stand <hi rend="italic">tieman</hi>. Dafür <hi rend="italic">warantum revocare</hi> Hn mon 2, 2. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Anefang 9</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The original had <hi rend="italic">tieman</hi>. In its place <hi rend="italic">warantum revocare</hi> Hn mon 2, 2. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Anefang 9</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IVAtr_7.robnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope></bibl><label>lacum</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">laccum</hi> M, Hk; <hi rend="italic">lactum</hi> Br.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
